turning overseas this morning Australian  police are praising bystanders who  helped end a deadly stabbing spree in  Sydney a man is accused of stabbing at  least two people and trying to attack  others in the city's financial district  overnight one woman is dead  police have not determined a motive but  say the suspect has a history of mental  illness  Lachlan Kennedy from our partner Network  ten in Australia is at the crime scene  this is usually one of the busiest  intersections in the heart of Sydney  city and today it was in lockdown this  afternoon when a man wearing a balaclava  and holding a large knife marched down  one of the streets before attacking a  woman who was sitting in a bar slashing  her in the back before running up this  street and jumping on the Front's of  cars at these traffic lights it was then  when members of the public saw him they  decided to gave give chase they ran  after him down another Street and when  they eventually got him they held him  there until police arrived  by using cut chairs from a coffee shop  and a milk crate placing it on his head  until police got there now it was only  after that man was arrested a 21 year  old from Western Sydney that police  sadly discovered a second crime scene a  21 year old woman stabbed to death in a  nearby apartment block the motives for  this attack are unknown but police say  they did find a USB stick near the man  on it there was information about mass  killing events including the  Christchurch massacre while they say say  at this stage while the man does have a  known history of mental illness he has  no known links to terrorism Gail thank  you very much Lachlan Kennedy from our  partner Network ten in Australia
 

